THIRD-PARTY SOFTWARE & DATA

This repository uses or depends on the following third-party tools and datasets.
Please cite each appropriately in any publication that uses this pipeline.

SOFTWARE
--------
Signac
  Stuart T, Srivastava A, Madad S, Lareau CA, Satija R (2021).
  "Single-cell chromatin state analysis with Signac."
  Nature Methods, 18, 1333–1341.
  https://doi.org/10.1038/s41592-021-01282-5

Seurat
  Hao Y, et al. (2021).
  "Integrated analysis of multimodal single-cell data."
  Cell, 184(13), 3573–3587.
  https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cell.2021.04.048

EnsDb.Hsapiens.v75 / ensembldb
  Rainer J, Cook CE, Wjst M (2019).
  "Enhancing positional candidate gene searches using ensembldb."
  Bioinformatics, 35(18), 3151–3153.
  https://doi.org/10.1093/bioinformatics/btz268

JASPAR2020
  Fornes O, et al. (2020).
  "JASPAR 2020: update of the open-access database of transcription factor
  binding profiles."
  Nucleic Acids Research, 48(D1), D87–D92.
  https://doi.org/10.1093/nar/gkz1001

chromVAR
  Schep AN, Wu B, Buenrostro JD, Greenleaf WJ (2017).
  "chromVAR: inferring transcription-factor-associated accessibility from
  single-cell epigenomic data."
  Nature Methods, 14, 975–978.
  https://doi.org/10.1038/nmeth.4401

DATA
----
10x Genomics PBMC 10k scATAC-seq (v1.0.1, hg19)
  10x Genomics (2019).
  "Chromatin Accessibility in PBMCs."
  https://www.10xgenomics.com/resources/datasets/
    10-k-peripheral-blood-mononuclear-cells-pbm-cs-from-a-healthy-donor-1-standard-1-0-1

ENCODE Blacklist Regions
  Amemiya HM, Kundaje A, Boyle AP (2019).
  "The ENCODE Blacklist: Identification of Problematic Regions of the Genome."
  Scientific Reports, 9, 9354.
  https://doi.org/10.1038/s41598-019-45839-z

